   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "dead_lettered is a VALUE deliveries.status can take, not a separate table - and the\nreason is what has to be true for a replay. A job scheduler's dead-lettered\noutbox row has nothing further to reference; a dead-lettered DELIVERY still needs\nits subscription, its event and its full attempt history intact and joinable\nexactly as they were. Moving it would mean either copying all of that across or\nleaving the real table pointing a foreign key into a second location, for no\nquery that actually benefits from the split.",
   "originalText": "dead_lettered is a VALUE deliveries.status can take, not a separate table - and the\nreason is what has to be true for a replay. A job scheduler's dead-lettered\noutbox row has nothing further to reference; a dead-lettered DELIVERY still needs\nits subscription, its event and its full attempt history intact and joinable\nexactly as they were. Moving it would mean either copying all of that across or\nleaving the real table pointing a foreign key into a second location, for no\nquery that actually benefits from the split.",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
