  },
  {
   "id": "u1n",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 838,
   "width": 591,
   "height": 90,
   "strokeColor": "#64748b",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100089,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700623,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "The fan-out step's actual concurrency-safety mechanism - the same role an\nidempotency_key's unique index plays in payments. Re-consuming the same bus\nmessage (a producer's own at-least-once redelivery, or the ingestion consumer's\ncrash-and-resume) attempts to insert the same pairs a second time, and the\nconstraint turns that into a CHEAP NO-OP INSERT FAILURE instead of a duplicate\ndelivery being fanned out and eventually double-sent to a real endpoint.",
   "originalText": "The fan-out step's actual concurrency-safety mechanism - the same role an\nidempotency_key's unique index plays in payments. Re-consuming the same bus\nmessage (a producer's own at-least-once redelivery, or the ingestion consumer's\ncrash-and-resume) attempts to insert the same pairs a second time, and the\nconstraint turns that into a CHEAP NO-OP INSERT FAILURE instead of a duplicate\ndelivery being fanned out and eventually double-sent to a real endpoint.",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "u2",
   "type": "rectangle",
