   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100123,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700861,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "ingested_events  ->  by raw event volume, not fan-out",
   "originalText": "ingested_events  ->  by raw event volume, not fan-out",
   "fontSize": 13,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "shd_1170",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 1196,
   "y": 1700,
   "width": 420,
   "height": 75,
   "strokeColor": "#64748b",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100124,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700868,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "deliveries outgrows ingested_events by roughly the ~1.6x\naverage fan-out factor - the same way a double-entry\nledger outgrows payment intents 2:1. Different systems,\nsame shape of reason to scale two tables independently\nrather than assume one scheme fits both.",
   "originalText": "deliveries outgrows ingested_events by roughly the ~1.6x\naverage fan-out factor - the same way a double-entry\nledger outgrows payment intents 2:1. Different systems,\nsame shape of reason to scale two tables independently\nrather than assume one scheme fits both.",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "en",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 1816,
   "width": 971,
   "height": 81,
   "strokeColor": "#047857",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100125,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700875,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "Trace the three modules together: 'one dead subscriber must never slow down another' is why the design fans out into one\n(event, subscription) row per match instead of resolving subscriptions at delivery time; that same requirement is why\n(subscription_id, sequence_number) exists here as a unique, indexed pair rather than an afterthought column - it is the\nconcrete mechanism that makes the ordering gate a single fast lookup instead of a scan. And sharding deliveries by\nsubscription_id, not by an event id or a hash, is what keeps that same lookup fast past billions of rows.",
   "originalText": "Trace the three modules together: 'one dead subscriber must never slow down another' is why the design fans out into one\n(event, subscription) row per match instead of resolving subscriptions at delivery time; that same requirement is why\n(subscription_id, sequence_number) exists here as a unique, indexed pair rather than an afterthought column - it is the\nconcrete mechanism that makes the ordering gate a single fast lookup instead of a scan. And sharding deliveries by\nsubscription_id, not by an event id or a hash, is what keeps that same lookup fast past billions of rows.",
   "fontSize": 13,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  }
 ],
